    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s, core %2$s</string>
    <string name="about_india">India operates NavIC, its regional constellation, and GAGAN, a GPS SBAS for aviation. ISRO states that NavIC does not provide integrity or safety-of-life support. GAGAN does. Original NavIC SPS bands are L5 and S. L1 started with NVS-01 on 29 May 2023. Android reports IRNSS as constellation 7 from API 29. usedInFix and C/N0 are visibility, not integrity. Qualcomm announced NavIC L1 on select Snapdragon platforms from the second half of 2024. DriftZero keeps a phone position alive when GNSS drops in tunnels, underpasses, parking decks, forested highways, and urban canyons. It uses the phone only. No OBD-II or vehicle computer connection.</string>
    <string name="about_limits_title">Limitations</string>
    <string name="about_limit_1">Not certified for safety-of-life or autonomous control.</string>
    <string name="about_limit_2">NavIC count is a chipset report, not integrity.</string>
    <string name="about_limit_3">Streets and routing use the network until a pack is installed.</string>
    <string name="about_limit_4">Drift grows without GNSS. The radius shows how much.</string>
    <string name="about_notices">Third-party notices</string>
